From 31facfa28aa2e49430e6cccf4ee9af0dd7c50c6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mira (mira/mira)" <hey2missmira@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 19:01:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] (be) snapshot-remote-unwind link libunwind-x86_64.a for
 remote-mode API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The variant TU `print_stack_snapshot_remote_unwind.cpp` calls
`unw_init_remote` / `unw_create_addr_space` / `unw_step` /
`unw_get_reg` against a custom address space. Those entry points
have real implementations only in `lib64/libunwind-x86_64.a` under
the `_Ux86_64_*` prefix. The default `lib64/libunwind.a` archive —
which the Doris build already links — ships the matching
`_ULx86_64_*` symbols as 6-byte stubs that return `-UNW_EINVAL`
(their bodies are compiled out under `UNW_LOCAL_ONLY` in
`src/x86_64/Linit_remote.c`). Verified empirically: `objdump -d` on
the archive's `_ULx86_64_init_remote` shows
`mov $0xfffffff8, %eax; ret` — six bytes, returns -8 (-UNW_EINVAL).

Gate on `CMAKE_BUILD_TARGET_ARCH == x86_64` because the per-arch
archive is named after the target ISA; the variant TU's accessors
hardcode x86_64 GPR layout via `REG_RAX` etc. and the variant ships
only on x86_64. The thirdparty build already produces
`libunwind-x86_64.a` whenever it builds `libunwind.a` (see
`thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh:build_libunwind`); no thirdparty
rebuild is needed.

Spec: docs/design/snapshot.md "Decisions" #12.

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
---
 be/cmake/thirdparty.cmake | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/be/cmake/thirdparty.cmake b/be/cmake/thirdparty.cmake
index 1dba907307d..8f9ce9d509e 100644
--- a/be/cmake/thirdparty.cmake
+++ b/be/cmake/thirdparty.cmake
@@ -87,6 +87,15 @@ endif()
 
 if (USE_UNWIND)
     add_thirdparty(libunwind LIBNAME "lib64/libunwind.a")
+    # libunwind.a is the local-only ("UNW_LOCAL_ONLY") archive; its
+    # `_ULx86_64_init_remote` is a 6-byte stub returning -UNW_EINVAL.
+    # The per-arch archive ships the real remote-mode implementation
+    # under the `_Ux86_64_*` prefix. snapshot-remote-unwind calls
+    # unw_init_remote/unw_step/unw_get_reg against a custom address
+    # space and needs those symbols at link time.
+    if ("${CMAKE_BUILD_TARGET_ARCH}" STREQUAL "x86_64")
+        add_thirdparty(libunwind-x86_64 LIBNAME "lib64/libunwind-x86_64.a")
+    endif()
 endif()
 
 add_thirdparty(grpc++_reflection LIB64)
